  "name": "Battle of Shiloh",
  "description": "The Battle of Shiloh was fought April 6-7, 1862, at Pittsburg Landing on the Tennessee River, in Hardin County, Tennessee. Confederate forces under Albert Sidney Johnston attacked Grant's Army of the Tennessee on April 6 and forced it back toward Pittsburg Landing. Johnston was killed that afternoon. Buell's Army of the Ohio arrived on April 7, and Beauregard, who had succeeded Johnston, withdrew toward Corinth.",
